  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Let $p$ and $q$ be the roots of the quadratic $x^2-mx+2$. If $p+\\frac{1}{q}$ and $q+\\frac{1}{p}$ are the roots of $x^2-dx+e$, then find the value of $e$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$e=\\frac{9}{2}$.\n\nUse the product of the transformed roots and $pq=2$.",
      "worked": "By Vieta’s formulas, $pq=2$. The product of the new roots is $e$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}e&=\\left(p+\\frac{1}{q}\\right)\\left(q+\\frac{1}{p}\\right)\\\\e&=pq+1+1+\\frac{1}{pq}\\\\e&=2+2+\\frac{1}{2}\\\\e&=\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
